#~ BorgBackup has no native Windows port. Operators who want the same
#~ properties (encrypted, deduplicated, repository-based, cross-platform
#~ restore) should deploy restic-windows or kopia-windows alongside their
#~ Linux borg hosts — both use a compatible mental model. This module is
#~ a marker so the borg role can be applied to a mixed fleet without
#~ erroring on Windows envoys; it installs nothing.
name: borg-windows

provides: [host-backup]

resources: []

# No native Windows BorgBackup. Install restic-windows or kopia-windows for
# the same use case. WSL2-hosted borg works but isn't supported here — the
# operator surface diverges enough that mixing those hosts into the borg
# role is misleading.
